module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_self_recursive_call_without_a_descending_argument_is_accepted

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode, RungRead, FoundBelowTheLadder, BelowCeiling }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

// EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY (DESIGN 6b): the compiler ACCEPTANCE PATH admits a self-recursive call whose
// recursive argument does not strictly descend. That is where the guarantee should have fired, not the scan. The
// DescentEvidence lattice (std.termination: Strict | NonIncreasing | DescentUnknown, with DescentUnknown the
// fail-closed bottom) is the evidence such a call should produce and be refused on; today nothing on the
// acceptance path reads it for self-recursion, so a non-descending self-call compiles and only the runtime paths
// react to it -- and they react badly.
data a_self_recursive_call_without_a_descending_argument_is_accepted: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_self_recursive_call_without_a_descending_argument_is_accepted" as NonEmptyStr,
  rung: RungRead {
    found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder,
    standing: BelowCeiling {
      current: FoundBelowTheLadder,
      ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed,
      blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt,
      trigger_capability: "an acceptance-path refusal on NonIncreasing/DescentUnknown for a self-recursive call whose argument does not strictly descend (std.termination DescentEvidence fail-closed bottom)",
    },
  },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: the acceptance path admits a self-recursive function whose recursive call passes its argument UNCHANGED. There is no strict-descent gate on the acceptance path for self-recursion, so a call that never descends compiles; only the runtime paths react, and they react badly.",
    "RECEIPT: gunbc.roadmap.roadmap_attempt_state_store.attempt_append_log_census_row (landed in #15471) recursed attempt_append_log_census_row(name: name) with the scalar `name` passed UNCHANGED, driving its scan over the module CONSTANT append_log_member_census rather than advancing a list parameter. It COMPILED and only diverged at RUNTIME as call-depth-exceeded. Because every prior claim looked up only the FIRST census member, the defect stayed green on main since #15471 with no live harm: the mint that calls it had no caller until this PR. The fix recurses over the tail (`rest`), which supplies the structural descent the acceptance path should have required.",
    "HARM: an accepted self-recursive function that never descends runs without a clean bound; for the census_row shape only the first row of the scan is ever examined, so any match at a later row is unreachable and the function never returns a result.",
    "DISCRIMINATOR: the DescentEvidence lattice in std.termination (Strict | NonIncreasing | DescentUnknown, DescentUnknown the fail-closed bottom) is the evidence such a call should yield; the fixed census_row (recurse on `rest`) descends strictly, while the accepted non-descending self-call is NonIncreasing/DescentUnknown and should be refused on the acceptance path.",
    "RUNG PER PATH (DESIGN 4b: the class rung is the MINIMUM across in-scope paths). INTERPRETER = Mitigatable: a non-descending self-call is refused as a typed CallDepthExceeded by the interpreter call-depth limit. NATIVE = below the ladder: per src/v1/05_emit_rust.dag emit_func_def, a TCO/TRMC-eligible self-call compiles to a LOOP via emit_typed_tco_body, so a non-descending self-call is an INFINITE LOOP (no bound, it never terminates); a non-TCO self-call compiles via emit_fn_def_non_tco with needs_stacker=true -- the segmented-stack stacker, which panics when it cannot grow (a process abort, not a typed refusal); and effectful_self_recursion_diagnostics refuses only EFFECTFUL non-TCO recursion, not the pure census_row shape. No native path gives a clean typed refusal.",
    "CLASS RUNG: the minimum across the in-scope paths is the native path (infinite loop / stacker panic), which is not a guarantee and not a typed refusal, so the class is FOUND BELOW THE LADDER; the interpreter's Mitigatable is recorded per-path but does not raise the class rung.",
    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- DESIGN 4/4b say the substrate should refuse a recursive call whose argument does not strictly descend, so the acceptance path is the earliest unjustified boundary for this class.",
    "NEXT TRIGGER: an acceptance-path refusal on NonIncreasing/DescentUnknown for self-recursive calls. Cite std.termination (the DescentEvidence fail-closed bottom) and the existing grounding claim gunbc complexity_contract_subject's DescentGroundedSccAnalysis as what is NOT yet that refusal: the former defines the fail-closed evidence, the latter grounds complexity, and neither refuses a non-descending self-recursive call on the acceptance path. Do not build the check in this PR.",
    "RESIDUAL, OUT OF SCOPE of the self-call repair (SelfCallWithoutDescent): mutual recursion (a calls b calls a) with no strictly-descending argument is the same acceptance-path gap, but it is NOT judged by the self-call advisory and stays below the ladder. Next trigger: a descent judgment over each call-graph cycle (the meet of DescentEvidence around the cycle), consuming std.termination DescentEvidence.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
